 the Ministry of Human Resource Development (MoE), Government of India, as an autonomous institution. SPAV is a premier Centrally Funded Technical Institution (CFTI) directly under the MoE, for excellence in the fields of Planning and Architecture. Although in its nascent stage, with experienced faculty and guest lectures by eminent visiting faculty and industry experts from all over the country, the quality of education imparted and its focus on research puts SPAV in the league of leading institutes in the country.</p>\n1195:            <a class=\"litem\" href=\"about.php\" target=\"_blank\"><i class=\"fas fa-link\"></i>SPAV Prospectus</a>\n1326:      The NCC Naval Wing Raising Ceremony was successfully held at the School of Planning and Architecture, Vijayawada on 20 August 2026. The ceremony marked an important milestone in strengthening NCC activities at the Institute and providing students with opportunities for leadership, discipline, character building, and exposure to naval traditions and activities.\n1388:     GOVERNMENT INITIATIVES / LOGO CAROUSEL\n1393:      <h2 class=\"sec-title\" style=\"font-size:26px;\">Government Initiatives</h2>\n1437:        <p class=\"ft-tagline\">An Institute of National Importance, focusing on excellence in Architecture and Planning since 2008.</p>\n1484:      <p>Content owned, maintained and updated by School of Planning and Architecture, Vijayawada (SPAV), An Institute of National Importance, Ministry of Education, Government of India.</p>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
